  "configuration_id": "config_002",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_001 (RNA, single profile, PCA) achieves 0.485 acc, and config_016 (multimodal, single profile, PCA+ResNet50, concat) achieves 0.527 acc, confirming that single-profile RNA is a reasonable baseline and that adding image helps modestly. However, we have zero evidence on whether multiprofile representations improve over single-profile. This is a fundamental architectural axis that, if positive, unlocks an entire branch of the search space (aggregation methods, multiprofile multimodal configs) and if negative, lets us discard roughly half the remaining configurations. config_002 (RNA-only, multiprofile, PCA, avgpool) is the cleanest possible test: it differs from config_001 only in profile setting (and the necessary aggregation), isolating the multiprofile effect without confounding with fusion, image encoder, or learned RNA encoders. It is also a simpler/faster model to train, making it budget-efficient. The result will directly inform whether subsequent experiments should prioritize multiprofile configurations (e.g., config_018, config_020) or remain in the single-profile regime."
}

